To cook perfect spaghetti, bring a large pot of water to a rolling boil and add a generous pinch of salt. Drop in the pasta and stir during the first minute so the strands do not stick. Cook until al dente, usually eight to ten minutes, then reserve a cup of the starchy water before draining. Toss the noodles in a pan with garlic, olive oil and chili flakes, adding splashes of pasta water until the sauce turns glossy. Finish with grated pecorino and fresh parsley.